cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this standard or its reference implementation, please cite it as below."
title: "MRFS: Marketplace Ranking Fairness Standard"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chandra"
    given-names: "Ieshika"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license:
  - "CC-BY-4.0"
  - "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ieshika/mrfs-standard"
abstract: "MRFS is a technical standard for auditing how marketplace ranking and recommendation systems distribute top-ranked positions across seller cohorts. It comprises a technical standard (metrics with interval-based statuses, an audit procedure for platform audits and external assessments, a reference governance charter and a data specification), an overview, a validation report, and a Python reference implementation with synthetic validation. It draws on research on fairness of exposure in rankings; its thresholds and defaults are identified as MRFS design choices."
keywords:
  - algorithmic fairness
  - marketplace ranking
  - audit protocol
  - AI governance
  - exposure fairness
# Concept DOI covering all versions of MRFS (not a version-specific DOI);
# Zenodo assigns each release its own version DOI under this concept DOI.
